   "reasoning_summary": "C7H9NO has DoU 4, which fits a benzene ring. There are six aromatic 13C signals (8-12 and 7), so the ring is unsymmetrical and para substitution is excluded. The 160.7 ppm signal is an aryl C-OMe, with OCH3 at 55.1/3.77. The 147.8 ppm signal is an aryl C-NH2, with NH2 as the 2H at 3.69. Three strongly shielded CH carbons (101.0, 103.9, 107.9) and one CH at 130.1 (1H 7.08, H5) are diagnostic of 1,3-donor substitution. The structure is therefore m-anisidine. The 1H count (4 ArH + 3 + 2) equals 9."
